      "side": 1,
      "message": "To be very honest, Greg\u0027s feedback was not ignored. Its just that we werent able to accommodate upstreaming all the patches in https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/q/topic:%22typec_vendor_hooks_6_1%22 and we just ran out of time. Also, pretty much all the new feature development (for ex.enabling DisplayPort amongst many others, landing fixes for interop issues across all dimensions: Charging, data, DisplayPort etc) was done without introducing additional vendor hook burden. We have always been diligent here.\n\nI can definitely commit to revisiting the patch to evaluate at the debugfs node option which had been proposed and see if this can be made to work with the build time default for this setting.",
